{
  "uid": "petclinic-risk",
  "title": "PetClinic \u2014 Risk Dashboard",
  "description": "Organised by RISK, not by technology. Each row is a failure mode this codebase is actually exposed to (no service layer, no pagination, Hikari max=10, an LLM-driven write surface on /mcp). Panels are the earliest signal for that specific risk.",
  "tags": [
    "petclinic",
    "risk",
    "slo"
  ],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "editable": true,
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "refresh": "10s",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-30m",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "service",
        "label": "Service",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "prometheus"
        },
        "query": "label_values(http_server_request_duration_seconds_count, service_name)",
        "refresh": 1,
        "current": {
          "text": "petclinic-backend",
          "value": "petclinic-backend"
        },
        "includeAll": false,
        "multi": false
      }
    ]
  },
  "annotations": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "Annotations & Alerts",
        "type": "dashboard",
        "builtIn": 1,
        "enable": true,
        "hide": true,
        "iconColor": "rgba(0, 211, 255, 1)"
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": 1,
      "title": "How to read this dashboard",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "Six rows, one **failure mode this codebase is actually exposed to** each \u2014 not six technologies. Every panel is the *earliest* signal for the risk named in its row header; hover a panel title for the code fact behind it.\n\nThe seed database holds 28 owners / 32 pets / 28 visits, so **RISK 1 and RISK 5 are latent** \u2014 they are measured as *ratios* and *slopes* precisely because absolute values look harmless at this scale. RISK 2, 3 and 4 are live: `/mcp` returns 5xx today, and the Hikari pool is capped at 10 connections."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "id": 100,
      "title": "RISK 1 \u2014 Unbounded reads & N+1 amplification (no service layer, no pagination)",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 4
      },
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "id": 101,
      "title": "DB queries per API request",
      "description": "Amplification factor: JDBC client spans \u00f7 HTTP requests. Controllers call repositories directly and MapStruct walks lazy associations, so one list call fans out into N selects. >3 means an N+1 is live; the seed DB has only 28 owners, so this stays invisible in latency until production data arrives.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 5
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum(rate(traces_spanmetrics_calls_total{service=\"$service\", span_kind=\"SPAN_KIND_CLIENT\", span_name!~\".*pg_.*\"}[$__rate_interval]))\n/\nclamp_min(sum(rate(http_server_request_duration_seconds_count{service_name=\"$service\", http_route!~\"/actuator.*\"}[$__rate_interval])), 0.0001)"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "justifyMode": "auto"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "none",
          "decimals": 1,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "#E0B400",
                "value": 3
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 8
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "id": 102,
      "title": "p95 latency \u2014 unbounded collection endpoints",
      "description": "GET /api/owners returns EVERY owner (findByLastNameStartingWith(\"\")) and GET /api/visits returns EVERY visit (findAllWithPetAndOwner). Neither is paginated, so p95 here grows linearly with table size forever. Watch the slope, not the value.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 10,
        "x": 4,
        "y": 5
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "legendFormat": "{{http_route}}",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (http_route, le) (rate(http_server_request_duration_seconds_bucket{service_name=\"$service\", http_route=~\"/api/owners|/api/visits|/api/vets|/api/pettypes\"}[$__rate_interval])))"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": true,
            "axisGridShow": true,
            "axisBorderShow": false
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "/api/owners"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "#5399d1"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "/api/visits"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "#795ea5"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "/api/vets"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "#009b8f"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "/api/pettypes"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "#8e4771"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "id": 103,
      "title": "SELECT rate by table",
      "description": "Which tables the fan-out actually hits. A spike on petclinic.visits / petclinic.pets while request rate is flat is the fingerprint of a lazy-association N+1.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 10,
        "x": 14,
        "y": 5
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "legendFormat": "{{span_name}}",
          "expr": "sum by (span_name) (rate(traces_spanmetrics_calls_total{service=\"$service\", span_kind=\"SPAN_KIND_CLIENT\", span_name=~\"SELECT petclinic\\\\.[a-z_]+\", span_name!~\".*pg_.*\"}[$__rate_interval]))"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": true,
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "normal",
              "group": "A"
            }
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "id": 200,
      "title": "RISK 2 \u2014 Error budget & API contract (the API is a product, not the SPA's back door)",
