    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "id": 502,
      "title": "Dead tuple ratio (vacuum pressure)",
      "description": "Dead \u00f7 total tuples. The MCP cancel_visit path hard-DELETEs rows and ./start-database.sh recreates the volume, so churn is real but autovacuum rarely gets tested. A climbing ratio means bloat: index scans slow down long before disk fills up.",
